  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Given \\(a_0=1,\\) \\(a_1=3,\\) and the general relation \\(a_n^2-a_{n-1}a_{n+1}=(-1)^n\\) for \\(n\\ge1.\\) Then \\(a_3\\) equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{13}{27}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(33\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(21\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(-17\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "33"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p40.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(n=1,\\) \\[ 3^2-(1)a_2=-1, \\] so \\(a_2=10.\\) For \\(n=2,\\) \\[ 10^2-3a_3=1, \\] which gives \\(a_3=33.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the recurrence first with \\(n=1\\) to find \\(a_2\\)",
        "Then use it with \\(n=2\\) to solve for \\(a_3\\)"
      ],
